Contrechamp — independent project derived from OpenMontage (TheCause/Contrechamp)

Contrechamp is a modified version of OpenMontage by calesthio,
https://github.com/calesthio/OpenMontage, and it is distributed under the
same licence: the GNU Affero General Public License, version 3 (see LICENSE).

Original work
  OpenMontage — Copyright (C) calesthio and the OpenMontage contributors.
  All credit for the original design, pipelines, tools and documentation
  goes to them.

Modifications
  Modified by Régis Rigaud (TheCause) since 27 September 2026, and named
  Contrechamp since 29 September 2026. The changes
  are recorded in this repository's git history; the main ones are described
  in docs/fork/ (lot 1: a final review that measures; lot 2: French first).

Adopted contributions
  Code taken from pull requests opened on the original project keeps its
  original authors in the git history, and the pull request is named in the
  commit message (cherry-pick -x) and in docs/fork/.

Inspiration
  The MCP server (openmontage_mcp/) follows the shape of the MCP server of
  openmontage-zh-mcp by noah-1106 (AGPL-3.0),
  https://github.com/noah-1106/openmontage-zh-mcp; it is rewritten, not
  copied (docs/fork/mcp-server.md).

As required by the AGPL, the complete corresponding source of this modified
version is this repository.
